From 4b21dbe7597c1f2a4e7702bd16ecb82a01dc79d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:07:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] MT-E1: Motor Test on PCI1203 follows golden -- jog,
 stop, home by drive type, reload motor data, motor list visibility

User rulings (EastSun 20260925):
- Jog = golden: Acm_AxSetExtDrive(1) + Acm_AxJog; stop = StopDec + SetExtDrive(0) (Stop1203 helper, all 9 stop sites).
- SetCmdPosition / SetActualPosition allowed: Reload Motor Data, and zeroing after a card-side home.
- Motion guards = golden exactly.
- Home branches by DRIVE (not machine type): DS402 / SERVOPACK -> Acm_AxHome 124/128 (no zeroing);
  other drive -> golden Acm_AxMoveHome MODE12 path + zero afterwards; unknown drive -> refuse.
- Motor list = golden bView rule (uMotorTest.cpp:145-390): forms/fMotorTest.cpp W906_MotorTestVisibility()
  (164 entries), published per Mot_Table row as "motorTestVisible" (looked up by motor index, as golden's
  layout loop does -- push order is not MotNo order).

Pci1203Control: internal kinds kCmdAxSetExtDrive / SetCmdPos / SetActPos / MoveHome (no wire names);
pci1203_control_gate allowlist now 23 calls (only the pre-existing WB_PUMP_1203_START_RING FAIL remains).
Tests: WebMotorAccess 195/0, MotorPoints_HT9050 passed; production_audit 0 changes.
macro_order_gate: 3 new / 3 expired = line drift in auto9045.h / ainarm9045_2x8_32.cpp (untouched since import), not this change.
Not yet verified on the machine: values/lamps read back, jog with servo off, home on a real axis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
